  "updated_at": "2026-05-18T16:34:07Z",
  "body": "**Update: Confirmed on v2.6.x documentation**\n\nThe [v2.6.x API reference](https://milvus.io/api-reference/restful/v2.6.x/v2/Collection%20(v2)/List.md) does **not** list the `Request-Timeout` header in any endpoint's parameter list. This is consistent with the v2.4.x documentation, which also removed this header.\n\nHowever, the header is still **functionally supported** by the server in v2.6.16 \u2014 both integer and non-integer values are accepted without validation, as described in this issue.\n\n**Documentation timeline:**\n| Version | `Request-Timeout` documented? | Header functional? |\n|---------|-------------------------------|-------------------|\n| [v2.3.x](https://milvus.io/api-reference/restful/v2.3.x/v2/Vector%20(v2)/Query.md) | \u2705 Yes (`integer` type) | \u2705 Yes |\n| v2.4.x | \u274c No (removed from docs) | \u2705 Yes |\n| [v2.6.x](https://milvus.io/api-reference/restful/v2.6.x/v2/Collection%20(v2)/List.md) | \u274c No (still not documented) | \u2705 Yes |\n\nThis creates two problems:\n1. **Type validation gap**: The header accepts non-integer values (float, string) without error, violating the original `integer` type constraint.\n2. **Documentation inconsistency**: The header works but is not documented since v2.4.x, making it an undocumented feature that users can only discover through v2.3.x docs or source code.\n\nThe bug (non-integer `Request-Timeout` accepted with `code: 0`) is still present in **v2.6.16**.",
  "author_association": "NONE",
